  "properties": {
    "require_edit_to_continue": "false",
    "encrypted": "false",
    "display_name": "Plant Growth",
    "long_instructions": "You’re constructing an artificial neuron to calculate how much a plant in your home will grow each week. The neuron has two inputs:\r\n\r\n- Input 1 represents **Grow Light**. Its value is 1 if the plant has a grow light and its value is 0 if there is no grow light.\r\n- Input 2 represents **Fertilizer**. Its value is 1 if the plant has fertilizer and its value is 0 if there is no fertilizer.\r\n\r\nYou are also given the following three pieces of training data:\r\n\r\nA. In a week where the plant had a grow light but no fertilizer, it grew 30 millimeters.\r\n\r\nB. In a week where the plant had no grow light and did have fertilizer, it grew 25 millimeters.\r\n\r\nC. In a week where the plant had a grow light and fertilizer, it grew 35 millimeters.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\n- In the widget, set the number of inputs to **2 inputs**.\r\n- In your activity guide, fill in the training data table based on the training data examples.\r\n- Experiment with weights and biases until you find values that correctly predict the output for all three sets of inputs in the training data.\r\n- Write down the weights and biases you found in the activity guide.\r\n",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Construct an artificial neuron to calculate how much a plant in your home will grow each week.",
